    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29530" root="عطر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِطْرٌ</span></b>  <i>Perfume; an odoriferous,</i> or <i>a fragrant,
substance;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طِيبٌ</span>: (S, A, O, K:) pl. [of
pauc.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْطَارٌ</span> (A) and [of mult.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُطُورٌ</span>. (A, O, K.)
[And ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِطَارَةٌ</span></b> , as used in the present day, and in
medical books, signifies <i>Perfumes</i> and <i>drugs:</i> see
an ex. voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صِيْدَلَةٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عِطْرُ الأَمَةِ</span> <i>A certain
berb:</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَفِرٌ</span>.]

